  "generated_text": "1. **Rewrite the expression inside the logarithm:**\n   \\[\n   216\\sqrt{6} = 216 \\cdot 6^{1/2}\n   \\]\n   Recognize that $216 = 6^3$:\n   \\[\n   216\\sqrt{6} = 6^3 \\cdot 6^{1/2} = 6^{3 + 1/2} = 6^{7/2}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Apply the logarithm property:**\n   \\[\n   \\log_{\\sqrt{6}} (216\\sqrt{6}) = \\log_{\\sqrt{6}} (6^{7/2})\n   \\]\n   Using the property $\\log_b b^c = c$:\n   \\[\n   \\log_{\\sqrt{6}} (6^{7/2}) = \\frac{7}{2}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Conclusion:**\n   \\[\n   \\log_{\\sqrt{6}} (216\\sqrt{6}) = \\frac{7}{2}\n   \\]\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{\\frac{7}{2}}$.",
